<title>RUSSIA: Russia's Norilsk shares drop over 15 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia's Norilsk shares drop over 15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Russian metals producer Norilsk Nickel dropped more than 15 percent at 1330 GMT on Tuesday, to $14.00 from Monday's closing $17.00.</p>
<p>Norilsk said earlier in the day it would ask shareholders to vote on doubling charter capital, by issuing around 126 million ordinary shares, at an extraordinary meeting scheduled for September 8. If approved, the measure would take effect after 30 days.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
